    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Watten is a sociable card game widely played across the Alps from Bavaria through the Austrian Tyrol to South Tyrol. Tradition holds it emerged in its present form in the Kingdom of Bavaria during the Napoleonic Wars, when allied French and Bavarian troops played in encampments; the name may come from French "va tout" (last trump) or from South Tyrolean Italian/Ladinian battere/báte (beating). It remains one of the most popular games in the Alpine region.',
